note=Cursor moved from 97a7d5e to f8e1d87 (Markdown web_fetch, DuckDuckGo, Dispatch efficiency and exit prompts; the previous sync also reflected the working tree of that day). The working tree of 2026-11-18 is reflected too, and goes into the next commit: markdown.rs rules (images, linked images, empty items, Wikipedia markers, superscripts, lost tables, site name), fetch.rs live test env vars, Dispatch stream owner (utils/streamOwner.ts) and Continue on a finished conversation (utils/dispatchContinue.ts), continuation line, cycle guard (dispatchGuards CYCLE_LIMIT), Dispatch prompt last line, summary prompt, repetition penalty step and display, Tools page copy. Docs updated: codebase-map (snapshot, Native tools, Dispatch, Key flows, Frontend chat, Stores, unit tests), known-issues (Dispatch, Native tools, Resolved). Not run by the sync: tests, tsc, cargo, the app; the cycle guard and Continue on a finished conversation are not verified in the app. manual-checklist.md, tasks.md and tasks-ordered.md were not touched by the sync. Earlier note (cursor moved from 8bfecbf to 97a7d5e): Dispatch phase B (background conversations; already documented at the 2026-11-16 sync; spot-checked at the commit: commands, title and notes limits, statuses, routes, startup sweep, empty-reply retries). Also reflected from the working tree, which goes into the next commit: web_fetch as Markdown (web/markdown.rs, dom_smoothie and dom_query crates), the DuckDuckGo web_search source (off by default), the tool result budget (tool_execute result_max_chars), the one exit prompt (utils/exitBlockers.ts, components/shell/ExitConfirmDialog.tsx, readRunningWork.ts), and the Dispatch efficiency work (sampling profile, prompt prefix, result budget, stall guard). Docs updated: codebase-map (snapshot, Stack, Background running, Exit prompt, Dispatch efficiency, Native tools web and search, IPC, unit tests), known-issues (Background running, Dispatch, Native tools, DuckDuckGo, Markdown). Not run by the sync: tests, tsc, cargo, the app. tasks.md and tasks-ordered.md are user-owned and not synced.
